<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<UserControl
    x:Class="Rudis.Shell.Regions.MediaBin"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:regions="using:Rudis.Shell.Regions"
    FontFamily="Calibri">

    <!--
      MediaBin — the region name is the handoff's, character-for-character
      (design_handoff_rudis_editor/README.md:33,122; CLAUDE.md rule 7).

      EVERY colour is a {StaticResource} token key from Theme/Tokens.xaml. A raw-hex
      literal in this file — INCLUDING IN A COMMENT — is a build FAILURE
      (MechanicalGatesTests.no_raw_hex_outside_the_token_dictionary).

      ═══ THE CONTROL, AND WHY (D-16 / D-03) ═══

      A GridView with an ItemsWrapGrid items panel. D-03's primary was the lighter
      repeater primitive; D-16 recorded that its pivot condition had been EVIDENCED
      (no built-in selection, no keyboard navigation, no phased container loading) and
      pre-approved either control provided the choice was RECORDED. It is, in full,
      with its evidence AND its two costs, in
      `.planning/phases/53-mediabin-inspector-regions/artifacts/53-02-control-choice.md`.
      That file was written BEFORE this one. SC-2 is verified by code inspection, so
      the record is part of the deliverable rather than a write-up of it.

      ═══ WHAT THIS FILE DOES NOT DO ═══

      It holds NO state. The level on screen is computed by `MediaBinLevel.ListLevel`
      from the MIRROR (rule 4: the backend owns the library; the renderer mirrors it),
      and every string a tile shows is decided by `MediaBinTileFactory` in the
      WinUI-free `Regions/MediaBin/` directory beside this file — which is where the
      parity claims are asserted without a window. The only view-state anywhere in this
      region is "which folder am I drilled into", exactly v6.0's `currentMediaFolder`.

      ═══ FOUR DELIBERATE v6.0-PARITY BOUNDARIES ═══

      REQUIREMENTS.md's Out of Scope forbids new features during the port, and
      53-CONTEXT § specifics says parity is judged against v6.0's ACTUAL behavior
      wherever it and the handoff differ. Each of these is a place they differ. They
      are written here so none of them reads later as an oversight:

        1. NO `MediaBin > Search` box. The handoff specs one (README:122), but
           `grep -n "search" frontend/src/main.ts frontend/index.html` finds no MediaBin
           Search anywhere in v6.0. Not ported.
        2. NO "12 clips - 240 MB" count/size line. v6.0 has none, and total bytes are
           not in the mirror — producing them would mean a per-file disk stat this
           phase has no reason to add.
        3. NO folder-CRUD affordances (create / rename / move / delete folder). The
           backend commands exist (crates/core/src/command.rs:333-354) but v6.0's UI
           never calls them; folders arrive ONLY via folder import. Wiring them is new
           capability, not parity (53-CONTEXT, Claude's Discretion).
        4. NO "importing" ghost-tile / progress-ring state. The handoff lists one;
           v6.0 has none.

      ═══ THREE RENDERING RULES, ALL PREVIOUSLY PAID FOR ═══

      · NO PUA icon-font codepoints. The glyphs come from `MediaBinTileFactory`
        (U+266A, U+1F5C0) and are plain Unicode. Windows 10 19045 ships no Segoe Fluent
        Icons and a pinned-but-absent family renders NOTHING AT ALL — Phase 50 measured
        this, twice.
      · NO width-responsive visual-state trigger. Phase 50 MEASURED that the obvious
        XAML mechanism never fires in this shell; responsive is a measured SizeChanged,
        as `Toolbar.xaml.cs`'s ApplyResponsiveLayout does. This region needs none at
        all: Column 0 is a fixed 486px (README:76), which is exactly the 3-column grid
        the handoff draws at the tile width below.
      · NO raw hex, anywhere, comments included.

      ═══ EVERY CONTROL HERE DRIVES SOMETHING REAL (rule 1) ═══

      Both import buttons raise events that `MainWindow` routes into the shell's ONE
      real import routine (Toolbar's). No button in this file ships with an inert
      handler; that is T-53-08's mitigation and CLAUDE.md rule 1's requirement.

      The double-tap gesture and its body landed TOGETHER, in plan 53-03, for exactly
      this reason: plan 53-02 deliberately shipped no handler at all rather than an
      empty one, because the only honest body is the real `rudis_transport load_preview`
      dispatch. It now exists, and it really moves the backend's source playback —
      see the two half-proofs recorded in MediaBin.xaml.cs's own header.
    -->

    <UserControl.Resources>

        <!-- ═══ The two header import buttons ═══
             v6.0's `#media-bin-import` pair (frontend/index.html:586-589), given the
             handoff's outlined-button treatment. An explicit token-only ControlTemplate
             per the 50-05 region pattern, so nothing inherits a WinUI system brush —
             which would be raw hex by proxy and would make the rule-7 gate meaningless.
             24px tall rather than the Toolbar's 28 so both fit the 36px header band
             the handoff draws for this row (README:66). -->
        <Style x:Key="MediaBinImportButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource text-primary}" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource border-strong}" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource radius-control}" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="9,0,9,0" />
            <Setter Property="Height" Value="24" />
            <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="11" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
            <Setter Property="FocusVisualPrimaryBrush" Value="{StaticResource accent-bright}" />
            <Setter Property="FocusVisualSecondaryBrush" Value="{StaticResource on-accent}" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <Setter.Value>
                    <ControlTemplate TargetType="Button">
                        <Border x:Name="Fill"
                                Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                                BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                                BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                                CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}"
                                Padding="{TemplateBinding Padding}">
                            <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Normal" />
                                    <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Fill.Background" Value="{StaticResource bg-elevated}" />
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Pressed">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Fill.Background" Value="{StaticResource bg-segment-active}" />
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Label.Foreground" Value="{StaticResource text-tertiary}" />
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                </VisualStateGroup>
                            </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                            <ContentPresenter x:Name="Label"
                                              Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                              Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"
                                              FontSize="{TemplateBinding FontSize}"
                                              FontWeight="{TemplateBinding FontWeight}"
                                              HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                              VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                        </Border>
                    </ControlTemplate>
                </Setter.Value>
            </Setter>
        </Style>

        <!-- ═══ One breadcrumb crumb ═══
             ⚠ The DISABLED visual here is deliberately BRIGHTER, not dimmer, and that
             inverts this shell's usual disabled treatment on purpose. The disabled
             crumb is the CURRENT level (v6.0 disables exactly that one, main.ts:493) —
             it is where the user IS, which the handoff's own trail reads as the most
             prominent word, not the least. Dimming it would have said "unavailable"
             about the only crumb that is definitely true. -->
        <Style x:Key="MediaBinCrumbButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource text-secondary}" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource radius-control}" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="4,0,4,0" />
            <Setter Property="Height" Value="20" />
            <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12" />
            <Setter Property="FocusVisualPrimaryBrush" Value="{StaticResource accent-bright}" />
            <Setter Property="FocusVisualSecondaryBrush" Value="{StaticResource on-accent}" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <Setter.Value>
                    <ControlTemplate TargetType="Button">
                        <Border x:Name="Fill"
                                Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                                CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}"
                                Padding="{TemplateBinding Padding}">
                            <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Normal" />
                                    <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Fill.Background" Value="{StaticResource bg-elevated}" />
                                            <Setter Target="Label.Foreground" Value="{StaticResource text-primary}" />
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Pressed">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Fill.Background" Value="{StaticResource bg-segment-active}" />
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Label.Foreground" Value="{StaticResource text-primary}" />
                                            <Setter Target="Label.FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                </VisualStateGroup>
                            </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                            <ContentPresenter x:Name="Label"
                                              Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                              Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"
                                              FontSize="{TemplateBinding FontSize}"
                                              HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                              VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                        </Border>
                    </ControlTemplate>
                </Setter.Value>
            </Setter>
        </Style>

    </UserControl.Resources>

    <Grid x:Name="MediaBinRoot" Background="{StaticResource bg-panel}">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="*" />
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <!-- ═══ Row 0 — the header band (README:66's 36px bottom-row header) ═══
             Region tag left, the two import affordances right. The handoff also puts a
             "12 clips - 240 MB" count here; boundary 2 above says why it is absent. -->
        <!-- The AutomationId is here for the same reason `Timeline.Toolbar` has one: it
             makes this band's TOP EDGE readable through UIA, so the handoff's "the divider
             reads as one clean cross" (README:75) is MEASURED against the Timeline band's
             top edge rather than judged from a screenshot. It is a container: it invokes
             nothing and takes no tab stop of its own. -->
        <Border x:Name="HeaderBar"
                Grid.Row="0"
                Height="36"
                AutomationProperties.AutomationId="MediaBin.Header"
                AutomationProperties.Name="MediaBin header"
                Background="{StaticResource bg-bar}"
                BorderBrush="{StaticResource border-hairline}"
                BorderThickness="0,0,0,1"
                Padding="11,0,11,0">
            <Grid VerticalAlignment="Center">

                <!-- Region tag: 10px / 800 / letter-spacing .08em / `text-faint`
                     (README:217). CharacterSpacing is in 1/1000 em, so .08em is 80 —
                     the same conversion TitleBar/Toolbar/Timeline already use. The
                     WORDS are the handoff's own for this region (README:124). -->
                <TextBlock x:Name="RegionTag"
                           Text="MEDIA FOLDER"
                           Foreground="{StaticResource text-faint}"
                           FontSize="10"
                           FontWeight="ExtraBold"
                           CharacterSpacing="80"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                           VerticalAlignment="Center"
                           AutomationProperties.AutomationId="MediaBin.RegionTag"
                           AutomationProperties.Name="MediaBin region" />

                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal"
                            Spacing="{StaticResource gap-toolbar}"
                            HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                            VerticalAlignment="Center">

                    <!-- v6.0's `#import-btn` (index.html:587). Routed by MainWindow into
                         Toolbar's ONE shared import routine — there is exactly one place
                         in this shell that talks to rudis_import_media, and this is not a
                         second one. -->
                    <Button x:Name="ImportMediaButton"
                            Style="{StaticResource MediaBinImportButtonStyle}"
                            Content="&#xFF0B; Import media…"
                            Click="OnImportMediaClick"
                            AutomationProperties.AutomationId="MediaBin.ImportMediaButton"
                            AutomationProperties.Name="Import media…"
                            ToolTipService.ToolTip="Import media files (Ctrl+I)" />

                    <!-- v6.0's `#import-folder-btn` (index.html:588) → rudis_import_media_folder.
                         D-15: Phase 50 left this affordance out DELIBERATELY and named its
                         owner in a code comment (MainWindow's drop handler: a dropped FOLDER
                         is ignored, and the recursion clamps "belong to whichever phase
                         surfaces folder import"). That phase is this one. -->
                    <Button x:Name="ImportFolderButton"
                            Style="{StaticResource MediaBinImportButtonStyle}"
                            Content="&#xFF0B; Import folder…"
                            Click="OnImportFolderClick"
                            AutomationProperties.AutomationId="MediaBin.ImportFolderButton"
                            AutomationProperties.Name="Import folder…"
                            ToolTipService.ToolTip="Import every media file in a folder" />
                </StackPanel>
            </Grid>
        </Border>

        <!-- ═══ Row 1 — the breadcrumb trail (D-04, v6.0 main.ts:474-502) ═══
             ONE level is on screen at a time; this is how the user walks back up. The
             crumbs are `Crumb` records from `MediaBinBreadcrumb.Build`, so what each one
             says and where it navigates is decided in the WinUI-free half and unit-tested
             there. The current crumb is disabled and cannot navigate to itself. -->
        <Border x:Name="BreadcrumbBar"
                Grid.Row="1"
                Background="{StaticResource bg-panel}"
                BorderBrush="{StaticResource border-hairline}"
                BorderThickness="0,0,0,1"
                Padding="9,5,9,5">
            <ItemsControl x:Name="Breadcrumb"
                          AutomationProperties.AutomationId="MediaBin.Breadcrumb"
                          AutomationProperties.Name="Media folder trail">
                <ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                    <ItemsPanelTemplate>
                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                    </ItemsPanelTemplate>
                </ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                    <DataTemplate x:DataType="regions:Crumb">
                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                            <!-- Empty for the first crumb; U+203A for every other one.
                                 Carried as a STRING by the record rather than as a
                                 visibility binding, so the rule lives in exactly one
                                 testable place and the template needs no converter. -->
                            <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind SeparatorText}"
                                       Foreground="{StaticResource text-faint}"
                                       FontSize="12"
                                       VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                            <Button Style="{StaticResource MediaBinCrumbButtonStyle}"
                                    Content="{x:Bind Label}"
                                    Tag="{x:Bind Path}"
                                    IsEnabled="{x:Bind CanNavigate}"
                                    Click="OnCrumbClick"
                                    AutomationProperties.AutomationId="{x:Bind AutomationId}"
                                    AutomationProperties.Name="{x:Bind Label}" />
                        </StackPanel>
                    </DataTemplate>
                </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
            </ItemsControl>
        </Border>

        <!-- ═══ Row 2 — the tile grid and the empty state, overlaid ═══ -->
        <Grid Grid.Row="2">

            <GridView x:Name="TileGrid"
                      AutomationProperties.AutomationId="MediaBin.Grid"
                      AutomationProperties.Name="Media tiles"
                      Background="Transparent"
                      BorderThickness="0"
                      Padding="12"
                      SelectionMode="Single"
                      IsItemClickEnabled="True"
                      ItemClick="OnTileClick"
                      SelectionChanged="OnSelectionChanged"
                      DoubleTapped="OnTileDoubleTapped"
                      ContainerContentChanging="OnContainerContentChanging"
                      ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollMode="Disabled"
                      ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                      ScrollViewer.VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">

                <!-- ═══ THE SELECTION RING — MEASURED, NOT GUESSED ═══
                     The handoff wants a selected tile to show an `accent` ring
                     (README:163, "2px accent outline / accent ring (tiles)").

                     The shipped GridViewItem template is a single native
                     ListViewItemPresenter whose selection visuals come from the theme
                     resource keys overridden below — read straight out of
                     Microsoft.WindowsAppSDK.WinUI 1.8.260709004's own generic.xaml
                     (DefaultGridViewItemStyle), NOT from memory. Its defaults draw a 2px
                     ring in the SYSTEM accent over a WinUI system fill, with a
                     check-mark v6.0 does not have. Retargeting the keys onto Rudis
                     tokens is therefore the smallest correct change, and it also closes
                     the rule-7 hole: without it this region would inherit WinUI system
                     brushes, which is raw hex by proxy.

                     A resource lookup inside a control template walks the realized
                     element's PARENT CHAIN, and this dictionary sits on that chain above
                     every container the control hosts — which is why the override is
                     here on the control rather than at app level, where it would also
                     have repainted any other list in the shell.

                     Full record, including the candidate held in reserve (an explicit
                     container ControlTemplate) and why it was not needed:
                     artifacts/53-02-control-choice.md. -->
                <GridView.Resources>
                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="GridViewItemBackground" Color="Transparent" />
                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="GridViewItemBackgroundPointerOver" Color="{StaticResource bg-elevated-color}" />
                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="GridViewItemBackgroundPressed" Color="{StaticResource bg-segment-active-color}" />
                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="GridViewItemBackgroundSelected" Color="{StaticResource bg-elevated-color}" />
                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="GridViewItemBackgroundSelectedPointerOver" Color="{StaticResource bg-elevated-color}" />
                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="GridViewItemBackgroundSelectedPressed" Color="{StaticResource bg-segment-active-color}" />

                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="GridViewItemSelectedBorderBrush" Color="{StaticResource accent-color}" />
                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="GridViewItemSelectedPointerOverBorderBrush" Color="{StaticResource accent-bright-color}" />
                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="GridViewItemSelectedPressedBorderBrush" Color="{StaticResource accent-color}" />
                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="GridViewItemSelectedInnerBorderBrush" Color="Transparent" />
                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="GridViewItemPointerOverBorderBrush" Color="{StaticResource border-strong-color}" />
                    <Thickness x:Key="GridViewItemSelectedBorderThickness">2</Thickness>

                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="GridViewItemForeground" Color="{StaticResource text-secondary-color}" />
                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="GridViewItemForegroundPointerOver" Color="{StaticResource text-primary-color}" />
                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="GridViewItemForegroundSelected" Color="{StaticResource text-primary-color}" />

                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="GridViewItemFocusVisualPrimaryBrush" Color="{StaticResource accent-bright-color}" />
                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="GridViewItemFocusVisualSecondaryBrush" Color="{StaticResource on-accent-color}" />
                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="GridViewItemFocusBorderBrush" Color="{StaticResource accent-bright-color}" />

                    <!-- v6.0 marks a selected tile with a ring and nothing else. The
                         platform's check-mark overlay is switched OFF rather than
                         restyled: it is a second selection language on the same tile. -->
                    <x:Boolean x:Key="GridViewItemSelectionCheckMarkVisualEnabled">False</x:Boolean>
                </GridView.Resources>

                <!-- Horizontal wrap = the handoff's 3-column grid (README:123). At the
                     fixed 486px column and the 140px tile below, three columns fall out
                     of the arithmetic rather than being pinned by a magic number, so the
                     layout still behaves if the column is ever made resizable
                     (README:180 wants 360-560px eventually).

                     CacheLength is the virtualization budget: one viewport's worth of
                     containers either side of the visible band. It is what makes the
                     realized-container count a function of the VIEWPORT rather than of
                     the bin — the property plan 53-04 measures numerically. -->
                <GridView.ItemsPanel>
                    <ItemsPanelTemplate>
                        <ItemsWrapGrid Orientation="Horizontal" CacheLength="1.0" />
                    </ItemsPanelTemplate>
                </GridView.ItemsPanel>

                <!-- BasedOn the platform default DELIBERATELY: an explicit container
                     style with no base would drop the default Template with it, and the
                     native presenter that draws the selection ring, the drag visuals and
                     the pressed states would go with it. Only the box model is
                     overridden here. -->
                <GridView.ItemContainerStyle>
                    <Style TargetType="GridViewItem" BasedOn="{StaticResource DefaultGridViewItemStyle}">
                        <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,0,8,8" />
                        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
                        <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="0" />
                        <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="0" />
                        <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
                        <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
                    </Style>
                </GridView.ItemContainerStyle>

                <!-- One tile. EVERY string below is a field of `MediaBinTile`, resolved
                     by `MediaBinTileFactory` and asserted by `MediaBinTileTests` without
                     a window — so "the tile shows what v6.0 shows" is a measurement.

                     ⚠ `Thumb.Source` is deliberately UNSET. Posters are loaded
                     imperatively by plan 53-03 (decode at tile size, off the UI thread —
                     D-07) under the phased-loading guard declared on the control above,
                     because a recycled container must be able to CANCEL a poster that is
                     no longer its own. A Source binding here could not. -->
                <GridView.ItemTemplate>
                    <DataTemplate x:DataType="regions:MediaBinTile">
                        <StackPanel Width="140"
                                    AutomationProperties.AutomationId="{x:Bind AutomationId}"
                                    AutomationProperties.Name="{x:Bind FullText}">
                            <Border Height="88"
                                    Background="{StaticResource bg-elevated}"
                                    CornerRadius="{StaticResource radius-clip}">
                                <Grid>
                                    <!-- The poster area, grouped so ONE property dims all of
                                         it at once. `ThumbArea.Opacity` is the handoff's
                                         "tile dimmed" (README:126), applied from the
                                         code-behind at the container's own phase 0 —
                                         `MediaBinOffline.DimOpacity`, which is the shell's
                                         existing dim rather than a second one.

                                         An OPACITY and not a colour: rule 7 gives the token
                                         dictionary every colour, and the handoff's table
                                         defines no disabled/warning ramp to dim TOWARD (the
                                         same wall plan 54-03 hit and declined to paper over
                                         with an invented amber — see Theme/Tokens.xaml). The
                                         honest dim under that rule reduces the element. -->
                                    <Grid x:Name="ThumbArea">
                                        <Image x:Name="Thumb" Stretch="UniformToFill" />
                                        <TextBlock x:Name="Glyph"
                                                   Text="{x:Bind PlaceholderGlyph}"
                                                   FontSize="24"
                                                   Foreground="{StaticResource text-tertiary}"
                                                   HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                                   VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                                        <Border Background="{StaticResource bg-bar}"
                                                CornerRadius="{StaticResource radius-clip}"
                                                Padding="4,0,4,0"
                                                Margin="0,0,4,4"
                                                HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                                                VerticalAlignment="Bottom">
                                            <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind BadgeText}"
                                                       FontSize="10"
                                                       Foreground="{StaticResource text-secondary}" />
                                        </Border>
                                    </Grid>

                                    <!-- ═══ Background work, per clip (TRUST-03, plan 63-04) ═══

                                         A SIBLING of the dimmed area, like the offline mark
                                         beneath it, so it is never faded by a state it is not
                                         about — and TOP-LEFT rather than centred, which is the
                                         whole of its relationship to that mark. The offline
                                         badge is the tile's HEADLINE: it is the only warning a
                                         beginner gets before pressing play that this clip will
                                         not play at all. This one says the app is busy on the
                                         user's behalf and nothing is wrong. It must not compete
                                         with it, so it takes the one corner the duration badge
                                         (bottom-right) and the ⚠ (centre) do not.

                                         The same neutral trio, and for the same recorded reason
                                         (plan 54-03): `bg-elevated` fill, `border-strong`
                                         border, `text-secondary` ink, `radius-clip` corner. No
                                         raw hex anywhere — rule 7 — and no invented "progress"
                                         colour, because the handoff's table names none.
                                         Lighter than the offline mark by weight and size
                                         (10px Normal against 11px SemiBold), which is the whole
                                         of the subordination.

                                         Text, tooltip, UIA name and AutomationId are set from
                                         the code-behind at phase 0 (ApplyProxyState), out of
                                         `MediaBinProxy`, so the copy lives in one asserted
                                         place instead of being re-typed here where no test can
                                         read it. -->
                                    <Border x:Name="ProxyBadge"
                                            Background="{StaticResource bg-elevated}"
                                            BorderBrush="{StaticResource border-strong}"
                                            BorderThickness="1"
                                            CornerRadius="{StaticResource radius-clip}"
                                            Padding="5,0,5,1"
                                            Margin="4,4,0,0"
                                            HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                            VerticalAlignment="Top"
                                            Visibility="Collapsed"
                                            AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Content">
                                        <!-- Plan 71-03 (TRUST-03): the badge now carries the
                                             engine's own number. A DETERMINATE ProgressBar
                                             (IsIndeterminate False) because that is what UIA
                                             exposes through RangeValue, so the value is read
                                             as a NUMBER rather than scraped from a sentence.
                                             Collapsed until the engine reports a running
                                             percent; AutomationId, Name and Value are set in
                                             ApplyProxyState. A 3px bar under the 10px label
                                             keeps the badge subordinate to the offline mark.
                                             Tokens only: `accent` fill on `border-strong`. -->
                                        <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical" Spacing="1">
                                            <TextBlock x:Name="ProxyBadgeText"
                                                       FontSize="10"
                                                       Foreground="{StaticResource text-secondary}"
                                                       TextWrapping="NoWrap" />
                                            <ProgressBar x:Name="ProxyProgress"
                                                         Minimum="0"
                                                         Maximum="100"
                                                         IsIndeterminate="False"
                                                         Height="3"
                                                         MinWidth="44"
                                                         Visibility="Collapsed"
                                                         Foreground="{StaticResource accent}"
                                                         Background="{StaticResource border-strong}"
                                                         AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Content" />
                                        </StackPanel>
                                    </Border>

                                    <!-- ═══ The offline / missing-file mark (README:126) ═══

                                         A SIBLING of the dimmed area, never a child, so the
                                         one thing that explains the dim is the one thing not
                                         faded by it. Centred rather than tucked into a
                                         corner: this is the tile's headline, not a second
                                         duration badge, and it is the only signal a beginner
                                         gets BEFORE pressing play that this clip will not
                                         play.

                                         The neutral trio — `bg-elevated` fill,
                                         `border-strong` border, `text-secondary` ink — is
                                         plan 54-03's recorded precedent for exactly this
                                         situation: the handoff describes a warning but its
                                         colour table names no warning token, and inventing
                                         one would break rule 7 from the other side.

                                         Text, tooltip, UIA name and AutomationId are set
                                         from the code-behind at phase 0 (ApplyOfflineState),
                                         out of `MediaBinOffline`, so the copy lives in one
                                         asserted place instead of being re-typed here where
                                         no test can read it. -->
                                    <Border x:Name="OfflineBadge"
                                            Background="{StaticResource bg-elevated}"
                                            BorderBrush="{StaticResource border-strong}"
                                            BorderThickness="1"
                                            CornerRadius="{StaticResource radius-clip}"
                                            Padding="6,1,6,2"
                                            HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                            VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                            Visibility="Collapsed"
                                            AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Content">
                                        <TextBlock x:Name="OfflineBadgeText"
                                                   FontSize="11"
                                                   FontWeight="SemiBold"
                                                   Foreground="{StaticResource text-secondary}"
                                                   TextWrapping="NoWrap" />
                                    </Border>
                                </Grid>
                            </Border>
                            <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind DisplayText}"
                                       ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind FullText}"
                                       Foreground="{StaticResource text-secondary}"
                                       FontSize="12"
                                       Margin="0,4,0,0"
                                       TextWrapping="NoWrap" />
                        </StackPanel>
                    </DataTemplate>
                </GridView.ItemTemplate>
            </GridView>

            <!-- ═══ The empty state ═══
                 TWO strings, because v6.0 has two (main.ts:509-510) and they answer two
                 different questions: an empty BIN needs an import, an empty FOLDER does
                 not. The text is set from the code-behind so the distinction is made
                 where the level is computed, never guessed here. -->
            <TextBlock x:Name="EmptyState"
                       Text="No media imported yet"
                       Foreground="{StaticResource text-tertiary}"
                       FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold"
                       Visibility="Collapsed"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       TextAlignment="Center"
                       AutomationProperties.AutomationId="MediaBin.EmptyState"
                       AutomationProperties.Name="No media imported yet" />
        </Grid>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
